Building the webport-core engine
================================

The only build provided is David Peng's Emscripten build:

    cd src
    ./build.sh          (build.bat on Windows)

which needs the Emscripten SDK (emcc) and writes ../web/ularn.js. The list
of EXPORTED_FUNCTIONS in build.sh is the interface a front end calls.

To use the engine from another front end (for example a native mobile app),
compile every .c file in src/ with your toolchain (the Emscripten-only bits
in ularn.c are skipped unless __EMSCRIPTEN__ is defined) and call the same
exported functions. Where the web version called showGame(), your front end
should draw the game once ULarnSetup() returns. ULarnSetup() starts a
game; the get_* functions read state; act()/move_world() and the prompt
callbacks advance it. The data files in data/ are read from a directory
named lib relative to the working directory.

For the original native TTY/X11/Windows/Amiga build, use the main branch.
